From e99163a210fe42ce7c47a1945711a12a8ed52646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:08:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] thunderbolt: apple: Flag 20 Gb/s for cables faster than
 Gen 3

The 20 Gb/s-per-lane cable flag was only set when the Enter_USB cable
speed field was exactly 3 (USB4 Gen 3). USB4 v2 cables report 4, so the
host router trained at 10 Gb/s per lane against a device at 20 and the
link never came up: the router firmware logged "Gen2/3 link error" about
30 times a second with "RT Broadcast LOCAL: gen=1" against "REMOTE:
gen=2".

Seen on a Mac Studio (M2 Ultra) with an ASM2464 enclosure, eudo
0x2687e000. With the flag set the firmware reports LOCAL gen=2, both
lanes enter CL0 and the device enumerates at 20 Gb/s, dual lane.
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
index 530008cc8..173a78c7a 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
@@ -843,7 +843,11 @@ static int apple_cio_tbt_switch_set(struct typec_thunderbolt_switch_dev *sw,
 		acio->target_cable_info = TB_VSE_CAP_APPLE_CABLE_INFO_PRESENT;
 		if (FIELD_GET(EUDO_CABLE_TYPE_MASK, data->usb4.eudo) != EUDO_CABLE_TYPE_PASSIVE)
 			acio->target_cable_info |= TB_VSE_CAP_APPLE_CABLE_INFO_ACTIVE_CABLE;
-		if (FIELD_GET(EUDO_CABLE_SPEED_MASK, data->usb4.eudo) == EUDO_CABLE_SPEED_USB4_GEN3)
+		/*
+		 * Cables rated above Gen 3 (USB4 v2 cables report speed 4) also
+		 * carry 20 Gb/s per lane, which is the most this router does.
+		 */
+		if (FIELD_GET(EUDO_CABLE_SPEED_MASK, data->usb4.eudo) >= EUDO_CABLE_SPEED_USB4_GEN3)
 			acio->target_cable_info |= TB_VSE_CAP_APPLE_CABLE_INFO_20_GBPS;
 		if (data->orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE)
 			acio->target_cable_info |= TB_VSE_CAP_APPLE_CABLE_INFO_ORIENTATION_REVERSE;
